<title>USA: U.S., Iraq war of words ahead of oil deal renewal.</title>
<headline>U.S., Iraq war of words ahead of oil deal renewal.</headline>
<byline>Patrick Connole</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A flurry of press-release diplomacy has started to brew ahead of next month's review for extending Iraq's &quot;oil-for-food-deal&quot; with the United Nations.</p>
<p>Despite expectations from Western diplomats for a renewal of the oil-for-food accord, recent days have witnessed an increasing war of words between Washington and Baghdad, which has support for a lessening of sanctions from Russia and China.</p>
</text>
